WEBVTT

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.740
This sucks.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.240
What?!

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.620
Chiharu Yoshikawa's an
insanely popular manga artist...

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.380
...who's sold over 10 million copies.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.720
It's too obvious that you thought...

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.000
...anything with that
name on it would pass.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.380
Don't be so arrogant, you idiot.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.520
When have I ever been arrogant?!

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.060
And, yes, even though we've
been friends for a long time,

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.070
I don't think you should talk
like that to the author!

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.340
To the author?

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.270
Talk like that?

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.270
That's what I mean by arrogant!

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:44.570
Well, it's true,

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.270
even I wasn't so sure about it this time.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.670
The more I thought about it though,

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.530
the more confused I got.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.650
I didn't have a choice...

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:57.290
...about forcing it out because
of the deadline, but...

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.190
The topic's not bad,

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.780
but the whole thing is too cramped.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:04.630
I can see that there's a lot you want to draw,

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.310
but you need to remember the readers.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.800
That's the most important scene.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:17.760
Why are you ruining it with a cheap joke?

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.440
You still don't get it?

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.690
Shut up, I got it!

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:36.870
Which reminds me...

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.570
Another bookstore
asked us to do a signing.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.310
I intend to reject them like always.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:44.600
Yeah, please do that.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.320
Tell them I'm sorry.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.470
I don't think anything would happen...

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.570
...if they found out you're male.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.800
I'm sure it would be a
big disappointment to all...

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.470
...the girls who think I'm female.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.970
It would certainly help me
to keep it under wraps.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:03.770
Huh?

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:04.970
What do you mean?

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:07.390
Nothing.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.260
Anyway, you wanted to get some inspiration at...

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.390
...the fireworks festival, right?

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.850
How about you go after you're
done with the manuscript?

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:14.660
All right!

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:17.000
I'm gonna have candy apples and octopus balls!

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:23.030
Are you going back to work after this?

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:25.250
No. The proofs are done.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.500
After this, I'm going straight home.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.510
Will you come over to my place then?

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.490
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.490
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:03.030
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:03.030
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.660
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.660
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:13.460
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:13.460
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:18.460
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:18.460
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.300
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.300
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:26.680
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:26.680
If I reach out my hand

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.060
hajimete no kimochi

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.060
Will you understand my feelings?

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:33.440
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:33.440
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:37.820
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:37.820
I love you more and more every second

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:43.950
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:43.950
We're still far from a happy ending

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:52.920
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:52.920
But I want to make it come true

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.380
tsuzuite yuku

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.380
Our story continues

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.140
This is good!

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.540
This is so delicious!

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:10.560
Tori, you're amazing! You're the best!

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.010
If you're done eating,

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:13.350
we'll correct the storyboards.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.760
Okay, okay! I told you I'd get it done today.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:26.880
Hey, Tori,

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.250
do you have a girlfriend or something like that?

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.370
Why do you ask?

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.750
Well, you were always popular with the girls.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.160
Now you work for Marukawa,

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.380
a hot-shot publishing company.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:44.380
I figured you'd be beating them off you with a stick!

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.410
Thanks to someone I won't name,

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:48.930
I don't have time to go on dates...

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.090
...or think about finding someone right now.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.490
But thanks for bringing it up.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.390
Sorry...

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:59.270
But there is someone I'm interested in.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:01.080
Really?

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.710
Tori's actually interested in someone.

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.530
So have you told them yet?

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:09.430
No.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.040
A secret crush?

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.340
You could say that.

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:16.320
So what's she like? Is she pretty?

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:17.100
What's she like?

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.040
You think it'll work out?

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.050
I don't think it'll be very rewarding...

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:31.710
Maybe I shouldn't have asked.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:34.930
I'll get that!

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:36.930
Hey, Chiaki!

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.190
I got the new The Kan!

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:40.320
Really?

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:42.070
That came out today?

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:44.270
And it's a limited edition, too!

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:45.430
Pretty sweet, huh?

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.230
This is awesome!

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.910
Let me borrow it when you're done.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:49.650
It's yours.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.370
I bought it for you.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.000
Really? It's really mine?!

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:55.150
Yoshino, where are your manners?

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:57.080
Oh, excuse me.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.580
I didn't know you were here, Hatori.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:01.340
I'm sure you didn't.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:06.520
Yanase, I thought you were
assisting at Satou's studio.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.100
The storyboard got delayed,

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.920
so I'm starting tomorrow.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.970
H-Huh? What's this tension?

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:16.360
You're one to talk, hanging around here.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:17.620
Why don't you go check on...

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:19.420
...the rough drafts at Satou's studio?

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.590
You don't have to tell me.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:21.980
I was just on my way.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:24.860
But you said you were done for the day.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:27.970
Just send me the storyboard
changes when you're done.

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:29.110
Okay...

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:38.310
I wonder why there's all this
tension when Tori and Yuu have...

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:40.250
...known each other since junior high.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.220
Did he make all this?

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.540
Yeah!

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:48.130
I've been dying for some real food.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.150
His sweet omelet is really the best!

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:54.010
He did my laundry, too.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:58.270
Aren't you a little too dependent on him?

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:05.400
If you're busy with work, I'll go home.

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:06.620
Okay...

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:09.200
Thanks for the book.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.280
I'm sorry you came all the way here...

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:14.010
No problem.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:16.290
I'll see you all the time
now that I'm an assistant,

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:19.040
and that's good enough for me!

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:20.130
Huh?

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:21.070
See ya!

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.550
What is up with those two?

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.800
Too dependent, huh?

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:51.200
So what am I supposed to do?

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:56.210
He's my editor, but he's also my friend.

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:58.250
He's my friend, but he's also my editor.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:02.080
I won't deny that the line is pretty vague.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:05.290
He...

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:10.320
Lately, he's stopped talking
about himself completely.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:22.230
Wait, he said there was
someone he's interested in.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:26.070
I don't think it'll be very rewarding...

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:40.880
I'll take the preview cover from here.

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:44.370
I'm sorry you had to come all the
way here to drop it off yourself.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:45.880
It's no problem.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:48.500
Otherwise I'd never get out.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:52.380
Hatori should be back any moment.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:53.510
Would you like to wait for him?

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:55.740
That's fine, thank you!

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:56.880
I'm going home.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:08:59.830
Goodbye!

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.630
It's raining!

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:31.420
Huh?

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:35.420
That's Yuu and...Tori.

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.130
What are they doing together?

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:40.040
Hey!

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:40.930
What the fuck?!

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:44.720
Hey, what are you doing?

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:09.390
That was him...right?

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:12.460
And that was definitely a kiss.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:16.670
So did Tori mean Yuu when he
said "not very rewarding"?

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:20.150
But he's a guy!

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:21.970
Are they all right with that?

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:23.970
Sir.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:25.260
Sir?

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:28.230
What should I do next?

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.120
Next?

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:31.480
Well, you could...

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:33.980
You could...

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:38.150
Sorry, I'll have something for you tomorrow.

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.240
You can leave now.

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:42.780
Yes, sir.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:44.870
See you tomorrow!

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.250
Goodbye!

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:51.000
Can you look this over?

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:51.980
Whoa!

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:53.990
What are you whoaing for?

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:55.890
Is this background okay?

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:57.880
It's perfect!

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:00.550
This is bad!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.140
I can't look him in the face!

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:03.400
And what should I do with it?

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:07.140
Well, um... Make it an afternoon scene.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.640
Jeez, now you tell me. How random.

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:13.200
Hey! I'm careful with the other people.

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:14.660
But you're Yuu...

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:19.400
So should I take that to mean you trust me?

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.410
Of course I do!

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:24.020
I don't need that until tomorrow,

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:25.550
so you can go home now, if you want.

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:27.130
What's wrong with you?

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:28.910
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.920
Did something happen
with you and Hatori?

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:35.540
With Tori? No, nothing happened.

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:38.800
Did Hatori say something about me?

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:42.140
L-L-L-Like what?!

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.180
This can't be happening.

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:47.310
I can't tell him that I know
how Tori feels about him.

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:49.060
Oh, well. Whatever.

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:50.370
See you tomorrow!

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:51.770
Yeah...

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:57.930
Is it possible that those two are going out?

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:01.400
Otherwise he wouldn't have said that.

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:06.300
They're both so secretive!

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.830
Why wasn't I told?

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:12.410
Maybe he didn't want to tell
me because they're both guys.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:16.010
Just stop thinking about it already!

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:18.820
I've got to concentrate on work,
and get this manuscript done!

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.360
Who the hell is that?!

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:26.390
Hello?

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:27.070
It's me.

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:28.130
How is it coming along?

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:30.970
T-Tori?!  Coming along?

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:32.520
Everything's coming along fine!

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:33.980
More than fine!

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:36.100
What the hell am I saying?

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.980
It's not fine at all!

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:39.260
All right.

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:41.090
I'll move things along on the assumption...

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:42.530
...that we'll submit right on the deadline.

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:45.520
What the hell? I just told you I was fine!

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:46.490
Don't get cocky!

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:48.870
Your productivity comes in waves.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:50.130
Even if it's good in the beginning,

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:51.870
you can fall into a slump.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:53.820
Yes...

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:55.740
Good luck.

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:56.880
I'll get it done!

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:58.320
Huh?

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:00.340
I can talk to him normally.

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:03.010
Tori?

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:04.610
What's wrong?

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:07.300
Was there something wrong
with the storyboard?

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:13.880
Yanase called me and he said
you were acting strange.

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:15.210
Is something going on?

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:18.520
Yuu called him.

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:20.840
Everything is completely fine!

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:22.010
I'm not acting strange at all!

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:23.710
All right then.

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:28.030
Did Yanase say something to you?

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:32.660
Did Hatori say something about me?

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:34.740
Yoshino?

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:35.660
Yeah?

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:39.670
He didn't say anything, no.

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:43.980
Uh, I'm going to take a bath.

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:44.670
Bye.

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:48.180
I can't believe it.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:52.180
The thing between them wasn't one-sided at all.

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:01.690
Why am I irritated?

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:09.360
It's pretty overwhelming to deal with college,

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:11.700
and drawing manga at the same time.

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:15.700
Then you should just become a manga author.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:21.100
But if I quit college, I won't
have any marketable skills.

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:23.400
Should you ever end up on the streets,

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:25.020
I'll take care of you.

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:43.100
Tori?!

00:14:55.300 --> 00:14:57.600
38.2 degrees...

00:14:57.860 --> 00:14:59.680
This sucks.

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:02.730
The manuscript's done, and the
first thing I do is catch a cold.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.290
This really, really sucks.

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:07.340
Thirty-two pages all done!

00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:08.150
We're done!

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:11.250
I thought that they'd drop us for sure this time.

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:16.170
I'll have to apologize to everyone once I'm better.

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:19.660
Maybe I'll take them out to eat somewhere.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:21.560
And then...

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:24.570
...there's Tori.

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:31.160
Didn't Tori and Yuu start going out?

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:33.820
Why did he do that to me?

00:15:35.090 --> 00:15:36.200
What the fuck?!

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:39.870
Maybe that was something aimed at Yuu?

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:41.430
Like a substitute?

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:44.600
Wait, what am I talking about?

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:48.210
Is that all I mean to Tori?

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:53.100
And what could Yuu possibly dislike about Tori?

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.910
He's pretty much the best guy out there!

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:00.180
They should be together,
if that's what they want.

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:04.480
Why do they have to get me involved?

00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:10.500
Too bad it's not me Tori's interested in.

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:13.240
What am I saying?!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.830
It's not like that at all!

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:16.240
But what I mean is...

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:22.520
How are you feeling?
If you're feeling bad, let me know,

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:23.500
and I'll have you checked out by a doctor I know.
You really saved me by making it to the end this time.

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:26.480
And the firework festival you wanted to use
as inspiration for next time is this weekend.
Do you want to go if you feel better?

00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:26.500
The firework festival...

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:39.150
Hey!

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:41.810
My voice just cracked...

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:43.100
Let's go.

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:45.780
Someone gave me a tip for a good spot.

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:46.980
O-Okay.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:54.740
What should I talk about?

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:56.740
This is so awkward.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:01.510
But he is my editor,

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:04.280
and Yuu's always coming in and out of my place.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:07.380
I guess that's why he wants to make up with me.

00:17:08.490 --> 00:17:11.060
This is a great spot for watching the fireworks.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.390
I-It is?

00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:14.640
Then let's sit down.

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:15.590
Your editor will change.

00:17:16.570 --> 00:17:17.380
What?

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:24.230
You mean it won't be you anymore?

00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:28.490
It was my fault the manuscript
was late this last time.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.460
I've lost your, the author's, trust,

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:34.260
and I took the next logical step.

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:36.470
Luckily,

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:39.200
there are many excellent editors in our department,

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:41.250
so if you have someone in mind, I could...

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:42.340
Now just a minute!

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:43.790
What's this, all of the sudden?

00:17:56.940 --> 00:17:58.680
I love you.

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:01.930
You probably already know that,

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:05.880
but I wanted to tell you myself.

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:10.270
I love you... You probably already...

00:18:10.670 --> 00:18:12.570
What is he talking about?

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:15.210
Sorry, but can you repeat that?

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:16.320
What did you just say?

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:21.090
But aren't you in love with Yuu?

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:23.330
He loves Yuu and Yuu loves him,

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.190
but they can't just admit it.

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:26.900
So even though they...

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:29.350
...started going out, it hasn't
been going too smoothly.

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:31.340
That's why Tori came to me and...

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:36.590
Why do I have to be in love
with him, of all people?

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.360
Am I wrong?

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:43.260
What about me or him gave
you such a disgusting idea?

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:49.840
Then...then Tori really is in love with me...

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:56.690
I got into this business because
I wanted to be close to you.

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.690
I was happy when I became your editor.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:04.150
I never even noticed.

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:06.350
I made sure you wouldn't.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:10.160
I mean, what would you think...

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:13.580
...if you found out how I truly felt about you?

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:15.990
Someone you only thought of as a friend.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:18.310
You'd think it was disgusting...

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:19.890
...that I've been in love with
you for twenty-eight years.

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:22.390
Of course I wouldn't!

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:24.620
Wait a minute.

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:26.890
I really don't find it disgusting at all.

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:30.580
I love you, too, Tori.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:34.400
Yeah. As a childhood friend.

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:38.830
You don't have to pretend.

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:40.400
I know how you feel.

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:44.720
Maybe I've been spoiled by
everything you do for me,

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:46.630
but...

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:50.230
But I don't want you to leave!

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:56.620
You'd be fine with someone else.

00:19:57.530 --> 00:20:01.800
You just think that because I happen to be right here.

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:03.240
Happen to be?

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.440
Who could replace Tori?

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:07.560
Don't worry.

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:11.090
We only have competent editors in our department.

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:12.560
Wait!

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:15.150
Why don't you try to kiss me again?

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:18.230
Then we could see if it works or not.

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:19.820
Just stop.

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:24.320
If I don't do something, he'll be gone!

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:26.560
No!

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:27.980
I don't want him to go!

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:29.640
All right...

00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:43.070
You're cold.

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:45.270
I can't help it.

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:46.960
It was the rain...

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:56.150
Chiaki...

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.980
Why do you have to go and use my name?

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:01.490
Say my name, too.

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:03.420
Your name?

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:04.760
Yeah.

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:06.970
Yoshiyuki.

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:11.450
Yes. Say it again.

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:14.000
Yoshiyuki...

00:21:14.780 --> 00:21:17.030
I love you, Chiaki.

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:21.510
This sucks.

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:22.760
Wha-?!

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:25.870
Then it's the editor's fault,
for giving bad direction!

00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:28.550
The first person I give it
to is just disappointing.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:31.920
That might be why I can't
help but lose my drive.

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:39.020
You'll be punished the next time you
put out something boring like this.

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:41.470
If you don't want that,

00:21:41.470 --> 00:21:43.530
then write something interesting!

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:47.650
What are you talking about?!

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:58.750
kimi o suki dakeja monotarinai

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:58.750
Simply liking you won't satisfy me

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:04.130
akogare dake ja ume kirenai

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:04.130
Simply admiring you won't satiate me

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:12.220
boku wa kimi o suki ni natta

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:12.220
I fell in love with you

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:15.730
yuugure no kaze no nioi

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:15.730
In a sunset, filled with the scent of the wind

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:20.650
boku wa omoidashite ureshiku naru

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:20.650
When I remember your voice and your smile

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:25.570
kimi no koe sono waraikata

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:25.570
I'm instantly happy

00:22:25.950 --> 00:22:29.870
boku wa kimi o suki ni natta

00:22:25.950 --> 00:22:29.870
I fell in love with you

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:33.790
dare ni mo mada ietenai

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:33.790
But I haven't been able to tell anyone yet

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:38.250
hitori omoidashite ureshiku naru

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:38.250
When I remember your voice and the way you talk

00:22:39.710 --> 00:22:42.750
sono koe shaberi kata

00:22:39.710 --> 00:22:42.750
Even though I'm alone I'll be happy

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:47.930
samishii kimochi potsuri

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:47.930
The feeling of loneliness... isolated

00:22:47.930 --> 00:22:51.350
sukina kimochi kirari

00:22:47.930 --> 00:22:51.350
The feeling of love... sparkling

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:56.850
futatsu kubetsu ga tsukanai boku wa

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:56.850
I'm unable to tell these two feelings apart

00:22:56.890 --> 00:23:01.480
yuugure ni kokoro tsuburete ku

00:22:56.890 --> 00:23:01.480
My heart is slowly crushed as the sun sets

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:05.860
kimi o suki dakeja monotarinai

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:05.860
Simply liking you won't satisfy me

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:10.320
akogare dake ja ume kirenai

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:10.320
Simply admiring you won't satiate me

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:14.700
asa no hikari ga afure dashitara

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:14.700
Once the morning light pours in

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:20.790
suki to yuou yuuki motte

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:20.790
I'll courageously say I love you

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:26.810
Marukawa publishing glossary!

00:23:26.810 --> 00:23:28.280
Today's word is manga assistant.

00:23:28.280 --> 00:23:30.390
A manga assistant's work starts once...

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:31.880
...the author finishes the manuscript.

00:23:31.880 --> 00:23:33.090
Backgrounds, pasting screentone,

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:34.490
erasing, finishing, and other things

00:23:34.490 --> 00:23:36.650
directly pertaining to the manga itself are obvious,

00:23:36.650 --> 00:23:38.500
but assistants also might be required...

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:41.000
...to go shopping and be on meal duty.
